From cc7d30adaeb80b39bdfd4eaf533973a36a6b05df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VAP Memory Optimization <noreply@example.com>
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 19:42:16 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] cel: build varEnvs lazily instead of materializing all 8
 combos

Prerequisite: patch 0001 (process-wide compiled-program cache). This patch
modifies the compiler struct / newCachedCompiler / compileFresh introduced
by 0001 and the "strings" import it adds. It also touches the same region
as patch 0010 ("lazify per-compiler varEnvs") and is mutually exclusive
with it -- 0004 keeps the per-compiler BuildNamespaceType/BuildRequestType
calls, 0010 additionally hoists those into process-wide singletons.

Today every `compiler` (one per `CompositedCompiler`, one per policy in the
absence of patch 0002) eagerly builds 8 EnvSets in `mustBuildEnvs` covering the
Cartesian product of {HasParams, HasAuthorizer, HasPatchTypes}. Each EnvSet is
two cel-go `cel.Env.Extend` clones, so the matrix costs 16 env clones per
compiler -- independent of how many of those combos a given policy will
actually use.

In production:
  - VAP uses 2 of 8 combos (validations vs messageExpressions differ only on
    HasAuthorizer; HasPatchTypes is MAP-only).
  - MAP uses up to 4 of 8.

That's 75% wasted matrix capacity per unique compiler instance. After patches
0001/0002, this is the dominant residual `F` cost paid by policies that 0002
cannot collapse (i.e. those whose variable signatures differ).

This patch converts `varEnvs` to a lazy memoized table keyed by
OptionalVariableDeclarations, materialized on first use via sync.Once-per-key.
The materialized table (envs) and the per-key once table (once) are held by
pointer on the compiler struct so the value-receiver compiler methods all
observe one shared table. Semantics are unchanged: createEnvForOpts is pure
with respect to its inputs, so memoization is observationally invisible.

Expected savings: ~3/4 of per-compiler env-clone heap on the 0002-miss path.
Estimated 1-4 GiB at 10,000 unique-shape policies.

Tested:
  go build  ./staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/admission/plugin/cel/...   OK
  go vet    ./staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/admission/plugin/cel/...   OK
  go test   ./staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/admission/plugin/cel/...           PASS
  go test   ./staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/admission/plugin/policy/...        PASS
